.Dd August 29, 2026
.Dt VIRTIO 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm virtio ,
.Nm virtio_mmio
.Nd Para-virtualized I/O in a virtual machine
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Ss Virtio Over MMIO
.Cd "virtio* at acpi?"
.Cd "virtio* at fdt?"
.Cd "virtio* at pv?"
.Ss Virtio Over PCI Bus
.Cd "virtio* at pci? dev ? function ?"
.Ss Virtio devices
.Cd "ld* at virtio?"
.Cd "vio9p* at virtio?"
.Cd "viocon* at virtio?"
.Cd "vioif* at virtio?"
.Cd "viogpu* at virtio?"
.Cd "viomb* at virtio?"
.Cd "viornd* at virtio?"
.Cd "vioscsi* at virtio?"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm virtio
is defined as an interface for efficient, standard and extensible I/O between
the hypervisor and the virtual machine.
The
.Nm virtio
device driver represents an emulated device that the hypervisor makes
available to the virtual machine.
.Pp
.Nm virtio_mmio
can be used in virtual environments without
.Xr pci 4
support, typically in embedded systems, exposing the device
through a simple memory-mapped register interface
instead of the
.Xr pci 4
device.
.Pp
The memory-mapped
.Xr virtio_mmio 4
and
.Xr virtio 4
over
.Xr pci 4
transport options share a common device model.
Most device operations, including, but not limited to, device initialization,
queue configuration, and buffer transfers, are common to both transports.
.Pp
The
.Nm virtio
driver provides the core infrastructure to communicate
with the hypervisor (called virtqueues) and supports the following devices:
.Pp
.Bl -tag -width Xr -compact
.It Xr ld 4
A disk device.
.It Xr vio9p 4
A 9P front-end device.
.It Xr viocon 4
A console device.
.It Xr vioif 4
An Ethernet device.
.It Xr viogpu 4
A GPU device.
.It Xr viomb 4
A pseudo-device to release memory back to the hypervisor.
.It Xr viornd 4
An entropy source.
.It Xr vioscsi 4
A SCSI adapter.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr acpi 4 ,
.Xr ld 4 ,
.Xr pci 4 ,
.Xr pv 4 ,
.Xr vio9p 4 ,
.Xr viocon 4 ,
.Xr viogpu 4 ,
.Xr vioif 4 ,
.Xr viomb 4 ,
.Xr viornd 4 ,
.Xr vioscsi 4
.Pp
.Rs
.%A Rusty Russell, IBM Corporation
